\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. My soul, repeat His praise
\par Whose mercies are so great,
\par Whose anger is so slow to rise,
\par So ready to abate.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. God will not always chide;
\par And when His strokes are felt,
\par His strokes are fewer than our crimes,
\par And lighter than our guilt.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. High as the heavens are raised
\par Above the ground  we tread,
\par So far the riches of His grace
\par Our highest thoughts exceed.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The pity of the Lord
\par To those that fear His name
\par Is such as tender parents feel;
\par He knows our feeble frame.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Our days are as the grass,
\par Or like the morning flower;
\par If one sharp blast sweep o'er the field,
\par It withers in an hour.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. But Thy compassions, Lord,
\par To endless years endure;
\par And children's children ever find
\par Thy words of promise sure.
\par                                  Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

